{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>He has told you</b> — This is the prophet's answer: <b>He has told you</b> — you, the man who says, 'With what shall I come before HaShem?' What is good in His eyes that you should do. And He does not ask for rams or your firstborn, but <b>only to do justice</b> — that you not do wrong against your fellow, nor wrong him in speech or in money, but <b>do kindness</b> with him to the full extent of your ability, and <b>walk humbly with HaShem</b> alone, that you walk in His ways with an undivided heart, the opposite of stiff-necked."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:09.945625376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}